ties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI KEISUKE</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGURE MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI, KEISUKE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGURE, MASAMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI KEISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGURE MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAKI, KEISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGURE, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIDA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A styrene resin material, especially a styrene resin composition, which is excellent in suitability for high-speed casting and stretchability and is suitable for use in extrusion molding, wherein the product of the melt index (MI) (unit: g/10 min) and the melt tension (MT) as measured under specific conditions (unit: g) is 20 or larger. An example of the material is a styrene resin composition comprising (A) 35 to 95 wt.% styrene polymer having a syndiotactic structure, (B) 5 to 50 wt.% specific polyethylene resin, and (C) 0 to 15 wt.% specific styrene/olefin copolymer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un matériau de résine styrénique, notamment une composition de résine styrénique, qui est tout à fait approprié au coulage haute vitesse et qui présente une excellente aptitude à l'étirage, et est également approprié pour être utilisé dans le moulage par extrusion. Le produit de l'indice (MI) de fluidité (unité : g/10 mn) et de la tension (MT) lors de la fusion telle que mesurée dans des conditions spécifiques (unité : g) est égal ou supérieur à 20. Le matériau cité en exemple est une composition de résine styrénique comprenant (A) 35 à 95 % en poids d'un polymère stryrénique ayant une structure syndiotactique, (B) 5 à 50 % en poids d'une résine polyéthylène spécifique et (C) 0 à 14 % en poids d'un copolymère styrénique/oléfinique spécifique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>